      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T16:42:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know we\u0027ve seen issues getting massive amounts of VDM:Attention messages to transmit HPD with MST docks at times, though I thought they usually resulted in the EC dropping messages from the TCPC\u0027s buffer.\n\nIn general, this is one of the trickiest parts about using our EC as a TCPM. If we allow the Attention messages to consume too much task time, then we\u0027ll be dropping motion sensor and/or keyboard data.  I would almost lean towards either trying to throttle the rate at which we handle the Attention messages, or trying to set up a way for them to process faster than other messages.",
      "parentUuid": "cbde39f3_1f3445ed",
      "revId": "35bf5e9d9e915d8673fb5714f11c20173b213892",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
